   3791  fc8d							; HotOverlapFlag — moved to bank2 (S5.3): fold-free body (HotOverlapBody)
   3792  fc8d							;   reads RoomRects directly via (FetchPtr),Y — 7 folds → 7 direct reads
   3793  fc8d							;   (one less push level on the hot path too). Entry tramp pinned $FE80
   3794  fc8d							;   (byte-identical bank0/bank2, moth pattern — the $FBF8-$FC48 pad window
   3795  fc8d							;   is full: 5 B left, a stub needs 6 B). Call sites below keep
   3796  fc8d							;   `jmp HotOverlapFlag` (tail: 0 push) and the C=1 contract: body ends
   3797  fc8d							;   `sec / jmp $FBF8` (ReturnPad), so the pad's rts pops the ORIGINAL
   3798  fc8d							;   caller's return. Full behavior docs moved with the body.
   3799  fc8d							;   Behavior: if the player's proposed tile range (CollisionCell*) overlaps
   3800  fc8d							;   any hot-only rect, set Temp bit 7 (HotBump), called from PlayerHitsMap
   3801  fc8d							;   HIT while CollisionCell* still describe the rejected position.
