   4250  fe0d							; ==============================================================================
   4251  fe0d							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   4252  fe0d							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   4253  fe0d							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   4254  fe0d							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   4255  fe0d							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   4256  fe0d							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   4257  fe0d							;
   4258  fe0d							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   4259  fe0d							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   4260  fe0d							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   4261  fe0d							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   4262  fe0d							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   4263  fe0d							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   4264  fe0d							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   4265  fe0d							;
   4266  fe0d							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   4267  fe0d							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   4268  fe0d							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   4269  fe0d							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   4270  fe0d							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
